To add a smooth transition effect for the hamburger menu toggle, you want two things:

1. **The hamburger icon animating** (transforming from ☰ to ✕ when opened).
2. **The navigation menu sliding/fading in and out smoothly.**

## HTML

```html
<header class="header">
  <div class="header__inner">
    <a href="/" class="header__logo">Brand</a>
    <button class="header__hamburger" aria-label="Toggle navigation" aria-expanded="false">
      <span></span>
      <span></span>
      <span></span>
    </button>
    <nav class="header__nav">
      <ul class="header__nav-list">
        <li><a href="/">Home</a></li>
        <li><a href="/products">Products</a></li>
        <li><a href="/about">About</a></li>
      </ul>
    </nav>
  </div>
</header>
```

## CSS

```css
.header {
  position: fixed;
  top: 0;
  left: 0;
  right: 0;
  width: 100%;
  z-index: 1000;
  background-color: #ffffff;
  box-shadow: 0 2px 6px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
}

.header__inner {
  max-width: 1200px;
  margin: 0 auto;
  padding: 16px 24px;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: space-between;
}

.header__logo {
  font-size: 1.25rem;
  font-weight: 700;
  text-decoration: none;
  color: #333;
}

/* Hamburger button */
.header__hamburger {
  display: none;
  flex-direction: column;
  justify-content: space-between;
  width: 30px;
  height: 21px;
  background: none;
  border: none;
  cursor: pointer;
  padding: 0;
}

/* The three bars */
.header__hamburger span {
  display: block;
  height: 2px;
  width: 100%;
  background-color: #333;
  border-radius: 2px;
  transition: transform 0.3s ease, opacity 0.3s ease; /* the animation */
}

/* Navigation menu */
.header__nav-list {
  display: none;
  flex-direction: column;
  align-items: center;
  width: 100%;
  padding: 20px;
  gap: 8px;
}

.header__nav a {
  text-decoration: none;
  color: #555;
  opacity: 0;               /* hidden before the menu opens */
  transform: translateY(-10px);
  transition: opacity 0.3s ease, transform 0.3s ease;
}

/* ---- Active (menu open) state ---- */
.header__nav.active {
  display: flex;
}

.header__nav.active .header__hamburger span:nth-child(1) {
  transform: translateY(8.5px) rotate(45deg); /* top bar → bottom-right */
}
.header__nav.active .header__hamburger span:nth-child(2) {
  opacity: 0;                                 /* middle bar disappears */
}
.header__nav.active .header__hamburger span:nth-child(3) {
  transform: translateY(-8.5px) rotate(-45deg); /* bottom bar → top-right */
}

/* Stagger the links so they appear one after another */
.header__nav.active .header__nav a:nth-child(1) { transition-delay: 0.1s; }
.header__nav.active .header__nav a:nth-child(2) { transition-delay: 0.2s; }
.header__nav.active .header__nav a:nth-child(3) { transition-delay: 0.3s; }

/* ---- Responsive ---- */
@media (max-width: 768px) {
  .header__hamburger {
    display: flex;
  }
}
```

## JavaScript

```javascript
const hamburger = document.querySelector('.header__hamburger');
const nav = document.querySelector('.header__nav');

function toggleNav() {
  const isOpen = nav.classList.toggle('active');
  hamburger.setAttribute('aria-expanded', String(isOpen)); // for accessibility
}

hamburger.addEventListener('click', toggleNav);
```

## How it works

- **`transition` on the `<span>` bars** — the top and bottom bars rotate into an ✕ shape, while the middle bar fades out. The `transform` and `opacity` transitions create the smooth motion.
- **`nth-child` selectors** target each bar individually so they can animate differently.
- **Staggered `transition-delay` on links** makes the menu items cascade in one after another for a polished feel.
- **`opacity: 0` + `transform` on links** ensures the menu doesn't "pop" into place — it fades and slides up as it opens.

## Tips

- Keep transitions between **150–400ms** for a natural feel; longer feels sluggish, shorter feels abrupt.
- Use `cubic-bezier()` for custom easing, e.g., `transition: transform 0.3s cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1);`.
- Always toggle `aria-expanded` so screen readers can announce the menu's open/closed state.

